(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Benchmark: KPZ at NLO (functions of p and of the external frequency w)\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"8dd0ff0c-1953-49c5-9bbc-4dc66feb91db"],

Cell["\<\
Kloss, Canet, Wschebor, PRE 86, 051124 (2012), Eqs. 43, 44, 49: the functions \
f_D, f_nu, f_lambda depend on (w, p) on the left-hand side; in the loop every \
function is at zero frequency, and w enters only through G(omega + w, Q). The \
f_D row is the even part in w of d_s Gamma(0,2), f_nu the even part of d_s \
Gamma(1,1)/(nu p^2), f_lambda the odd part of d_s Gamma(1,1) divided by i w \
(design/NLOPIPELINE.md). With f_lambda = 1 this is KCW's LO, which BMWflow \
calls \"NLO\".\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"771c7c88-d5cd-4577-98af-ccffba4035f0"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"];
kpznloDir = ExpandFileName[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/benchmarks/KPZNLO\
\"];
Block[{Print}, Get[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[kpznloDir], #, \"Pipeline.wl\
\"}]] & /@ {\"KPZLO\", \"KPZLOLambda\"}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"87083a81-236b-4eb2-81ee-8d1d13699620"],

Cell["1. NLO equations", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2429c718-2298-4d23-9724-8dd6f038f6ea"],

Cell["\<\
The LO loops of benchmarks/KPZLO and KPZLOLambda, with \"ExternalFrequency\" \
-> True. The card shows the NLO checks: every row at w = 0 equals its LO row; \
Gamma(hbar, hbar) is even in w; the f_lambda row vanishes at p = 0 and the \
p^0 order of the f_nu row vanishes, for every w.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"09ed3775-8090-4214-b40c-0ca8be3c058c"],

Cell["\<\
kpzlamnloEquations = BuildLOEquations[kpzlamLoops, kpzlamSymmetries, \
\"ExternalFrequency\" -> True];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b62b6e30-6c4f-4261-980e-81aa7875a1d4"],

Cell["RunOracle[kpzlamnloEquations];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3e2ff64f-225a-4dd0-92a6-925d96d170a8"],

Cell["\<\
kpzlamnloAdim = AdimensionalEquations[kpzlamnloEquations, kpzlamDims];
kpzlamnloAdim[\"Linear\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0e135c3f-dce3-471a-b458-479da3cf59d2"],

Cell["\<\
kpznloEquations = BuildLOEquations[kpzloLoops, kpzloSymmetries, \
\"ExternalFrequency\" -> True];
kpznloAdim = AdimensionalEquations[kpznloEquations, kpzloDims];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3f43e197-b26b-4bf8-a6ce-5a1dbca32a3e"],

Cell["2. References and checks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ebc87c42-d032-4412-b6c1-9aaf317351a8"],

Cell["\<\
Generic f_lambda and w against BMWflow's NLO kernels with f_lambda slots \
(Reference.wl); the w = 0 slice against the LO benchmarks; the linear part \
against KCW Eq. 56; the oracle at w != 0.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68fcb649-8280-4c9a-ab21-333c3b3c0c62"],

Cell["\<\
Get[FileNameJoin[{kpznloDir, #}]] & /@ {\"Reference.wl\", \"Checks.wl\"};
kpznloResults = kpznloChecks[];
kpznloSummary[kpznloResults]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"08ba1e65-4796-452e-9ca7-9abceb6b6095"],

Cell["\<\
If[AllTrue[kpznloResults, #Pass &], \"all checks pass\", Abort[]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"077cf373-1b7b-4b12-b147-843c550199d8"],

Cell["3. Export (contract v4)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8fde1c38-437a-469a-8857-bb2e24743511"],

Cell["\<\
ExportPython[kpzlamnloAdim, \"G\" -> alamk^2, \"Model\" -> \"KPZLambda\", \
\"File\" -> FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"KPZLambda_NLO.py\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9289ebef-5f0c-4914-981a-306025530263"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"0675b444-b4ac-42da-b384-bc76edabd5c4"
]
(* End of Notebook Content *)

